<title>GERMANY: German inland gas oil eases with world markets.</title>
<headline>German inland gas oil eases with world markets.</headline>
<text>
<p>(DLR/DM=1.5125)   DM/100 LTRS     DLRS/100 LTRS   LAST DM</p>
<p> HAMBURG	     36.10/36.50     23.87/24.13     36.80/37.20</p>
<p> BREMEN		36.10/36.50     23.87/24.13     36.80/37.20</p>
<p> DUISBURG	    36.40/36.80     24.07/24.33     37.00/37.30</p>
<p> FRANKFURT	   37.00/37.20     24.46/24.60     37.60/37.90</p>
<p> KARLSRUHE	   37.20/37.50     24.60/24.79     38.00/39.00</p>
<p> INGOLSTADT	  38.00/38.20     25.12/25.26     38.00/39.00</p>
<p>German inland gas oil prices eased again on Monday due to recent sharp falls in world markets, suppliers said. Demand was weak and the mark fell against the dollar.</p>
<p>-- Tom Ashby, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8145</p>
</text>
